   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator x - 2 has limit 0 as x approaches 2, and the denominator x - sqrt(x + 2) has limit 2 - sqrt(4) = 0, so the form is zero over zero.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Multiply numerator and denominator by x + sqrt(x + 2). The denominator becomes x^2 - (x + 2) = x^2 - x - 2 = (x - 2)(x + 1), so the quotient is (x - 2)(x + sqrt(x + 2))/((x - 2)(x + 1)).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  "x",
                  2
               ],
               [
                  "Add",
                  "x",
                  [
                     "Sqrt",
                     [
                        "Add",
                        "x",
                        2
                     ]
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  "x",
                  2
               ],
               [
                  "Add",
                  "x",
                  1
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "For x not equal to 2 the factor x - 2 divides out, leaving (x + sqrt(x + 2))/(x + 1).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               [
